  "notes": [
   "The booklet is a single page showing steps 1-9. The pictures are small and dark, so some placements are best guesses.",
   "Steps 1-4 appear to be built upside down and flipped at step 4.",
   "The pieces in steps 1-4 are assumed to be black 2x6 plate (b1), dark gray 2x6 plate (b2), a side-handle plate (b3) and two pin bricks (b4, b5) with a 1x2 plate (b6) between them.",
   "Step 5 is assumed to add the red 2x3 plate, the black 2x4 plate overhanging the rear, and two side-handle plates for the air scoops. Step 6 adds the black 2x2 plate, the two scoops and the front grille assembly.",
   "The front grille assembly (callout 2) is assumed to be a bracket, a 1x2 plate, two trans-clear round plates and the grille tile.",
   "Step 7 is assumed to add the curved hood 50948 over the red plate. Step 8 puts the 2x2 groove tile over the hood studs and the black 2x2 plate. Step 9 adds the four wheels, four tyres and the stickers.",
   "Pieces from the parts list that I could not place from this page: lego-45677 (curved wedge), the dark gray lego-3020 2x4 plate, one black lego-3022 2x2 plate and one dark gray lego-3023 1x2 plate. The booklet does not clearly show them, so they are not in the graph.",
   "The parts-list quantities (3 handle plates, 2 round plates) are respected only partly: b3, b9 and b10 are the three handle plates.",
   "The sticker sheet is attached to the hood for completeness.",
   "Page 2 is the alternate combined build 8655 + 8658 (steps 7-11). It starts from the finished 8658 chassis and adds red, white and black pieces that belong to set 8655.",
   "None of those pieces are in the 8658 parts list, so I did not record them. Nothing from this page is added.",
   "The 8658 model itself was already fully recorded from page 1.",
   "The checker said three pieces from the parts list were missing: the dark gray lego-3020 2x4 plate, a second black lego-3022 2x2 plate and the lego-45677 curved wedge. I added them as b30, b31 and b32.",
   "The booklet pictures are too small and dark to show exactly where these three go, so their positions are best guesses: b30 on the pin bricks and middle plate, b31 beside b11 on the black 2x4, b32 on b30.",
   "These are additions only. All earlier pieces and edges stay as given on page 1.",
   "Page 2 is the combined 8655 + 8658 build. Its pieces are not in the 8658 parts list, so they are still not recorded. The earlier note that the three pieces could not be placed is now replaced by this one.",
   "The Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors need authorization before they can be used. This session is non-interactive, so I could not do that. You can authorize them in your claude.ai connector settings. They are not needed for this graph."
  ]
 },
